; ============================================================================
; CSpect debug script — G46(b) Probe 11 — capture state at the bank-flip
; sentinel RET ($3D00) and at the NR-pair-set helper entry ($0082).
;
; Why this BP:
;   In jnext (both bypass and non-bypass) the supervisor RETs to $0000,
;   NOPs through to $0008, hits a delayed-AUTOMAP RST 8 trap, runs DivMMC
;   ROM bytes that JP into DivMMC RAM bank 0, NOPs through ~2400 zero
;   bytes, hits a sentinel RET at $3D00 and pops $0082 as the
;   continuation. $0082 is a DivMMC firmware helper that hard-codes
;   NR_56=$0E, NR_57=$0F.
;
;   In jnext the supervisor stalls at $20E6 with NR_57=$0F. CSpect at
;   $20E6 has NR_57=$10. Same enNxtmmc.rom in both. Same supervisor.
;   So the divergence MUST be in WHAT VALUE IS PUSHED before this chain.
;   $3D00 is exactly where that pushed value gets popped — capturing
;   state there directly reveals the divergence.
;
; HOW TO USE:
;   1. Boot NextZXOS in CSpect normally (TBBlue splash → SPACEBAR / wait)
;   2. Stop boot EARLY — as soon as TBBlue splash appears or right after,
;      open the debugger (F1) BEFORE NextZXOS welcome screen renders.
;      We want the FIRST time supervisor reaches $3D00.
;      Alternative: set the BPs first then hard-reset CSpect.
;   3. Set the breakpoints below, then `g` to continue.
;   4. When BP fires, run all the dump commands. Save the scrollback.
;   5. `g` again to let it run, capture next hit if useful.
;
; CSpect debugger commands (v2.x reference):
;   bp <addr>     — set breakpoint
;   bp off <addr> — clear breakpoint
;   g             — go (continue execution)
;   r             — show all Z80 registers
;   m <addr> <n>  — memory dump n bytes from <addr>
;   nr <reg>      — read NextReg <reg>
; ============================================================================


; ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
; STEP 1 — set the two breakpoints
; ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
; Primary: sentinel RET in DivMMC RAM bank 0
bp 3d00

; Fallback: NR-pair-set helper entry in DivMMC firmware
bp 0082

; ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
; STEP 2 — hard-reset CSpect (Ctrl+F5 or restart) and let it run
; (the BPs were set before reset; they should persist)
; ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
g


; ============================================================================
; STEP 3 — when BP fires (FIRST HIT), run the commands below.
; Save the entire debugger output buffer / scrollback.
;
; IMPORTANT: note WHICH BP fired (PC=$3D00 or PC=$0082) and at what time
; relative to boot (= before TBBlue splash, after splash, after NextZXOS
; logo, after welcome screen, etc.). The relative timing matters.
; ============================================================================


; --- 3a. Z80 register file ---
; Critical: AF, SP. AF tells us what was POPed earlier (= the pushed
; continuation that determines NR_57 outcome). SP tells us how deep
; the call chain is.
r


; --- 3b. Stack contents — 32 bytes from SP ---
; If BP fired at $3D00: top of stack is the value about to be POPed by RET.
;   - In jnext this is $0082 → NR_57=$0F path.
;   - In CSpect we expect this to be DIFFERENT (e.g. $0080 → no NR write,
;     or some other DivMMC firmware entry that produces NR_57=$10).
; If BP fired at $0082: top of stack is the return address from CALL/RST.
m sp 32


; --- 3c. NextReg state — focus on the bank-mapping registers ---
nr 04
nr 50
nr 51
nr 52
nr 53
nr 54
nr 55
nr 56
nr 57
nr 8c
nr 8e
nr B8
nr B9
nr BA
nr BB


; --- 3d. Slot 0 first 256 bytes — what's currently mapped there? ---
; If BP at $3D00: slot 0 should be enNxtmmc.rom (DivMMC AUTOMAP active).
; In jnext we get a 100% match with enNxtmmc.rom. Verify CSpect matches.
m 0000 256


; --- 3e. Slot 1 around the NOP sled ---
; In jnext slot 1 = empty DivMMC RAM bank 0 (zeros + sentinel c9 at $3D00).
; If CSpect has non-zero data at $3CC9-$3CFF, the supervisor's sled would
; behave differently → different path → different stack push.
m 3CE0 64
m 3D00 32


; --- 3f. NextZXOS sysvar block at $5B00..$5BFF ---
; Should match jnext's (already known). Sanity check.
m 5B00 256


; --- 3g. Stack-area snapshot near $5BFF (= NextZXOS supervisor stack top) ---
; Lower addresses reveal pushed return frames. Top is at SP — see 3b.
m 5B80 128


; --- 3h. DivMMC RAM banks: requires CSpect-specific syntax ---
; If CSpect supports direct DivMMC RAM access:
;   - DivMMC RAM banks 0..15 (each 8K)
; If unavailable, dump just bank 0 by activating CONMEM via port $E3:
;   This is RISKY mid-execution; skip unless you know what you're doing.


; ============================================================================
; STEP 4 — continue and capture next hit (OPTIONAL)
; ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
; After saving the FIRST-hit dump:
;   g            ; continue
; If BP fires again repeat step 3, save separately.
;
; If the welcome screen renders without further BP fires: the FIRST hit
; was the only relevant one and we have the data.
;
; If BP fires many times: capture 2-3 hits and note which produced
; NR_57 transitions.
; ============================================================================


; ============================================================================
; STEP 5 — disable BPs and let it boot
; ============================================================================
bp off 3d00
bp off 0082
g
